  "what_this_is": "The models a person's Mac serves for their Trillion (kinds local-model-server, local-model-job, local-model-classifier and local-model-offer), read by computer/local-models.mjs and, for the model a job is meant to be answered by, src/model-routes.mjs. A `local-model-server` row is a chat server asked in the OpenAI chat shape; a `local-model-job` row (its id is the job's name) says which servers answer a job, in order, and how many tokens a reply may use; a `local-model-classifier` row answers yes-or-no questions; a `local-model-offer` row is a model the person can be offered to download. The model server's own address, the disk it needs and the words stay in computer/local-models.json. Another runtime is another row.",
